            "review_text": "Wander51943478564\n4 contributions\n0\nIf you’ve been looking for a “real restaurant” during your trip to Natrah, this is the answer!\nMar 2025 • Family\nIt is also easy to reach near Golden Coast, and is in the heart of the city. I went by and wondered if there were a lot of locals visiting, but I was really pleased.\n\nThe one I ordered today was the Kitchen + Water Cool + Kitchen Kim.\n\nTriangle: The bitterly chopped meat is well baked in the charcoal, and it is an apparent splash, an insane touch! The quality of the meat was excellent, and the Korean salad vegetables and salads were prepared, so the taste was the same as in Korea.\n\nWater cold: After eating meat, make it cool! They are clean and have a deep water flavor, so they fit really well in hot natron weather.\n\nKim: It came out loudly, and the inside was touching. Kim Jong-un had enough, so I gave him just one.\n\nOverall, the food is really quality, perfect when you miss a meal.\n\nRecommended for those who are looking for a genuine snack restaurant!\n\nEspecially the local taste, there are quite a few local guests passing by. It's a Korean restaurant, but it's also a place with a good Vietnamese atmosphere.\n\nI think it's a restaurant in Natrang, a local restaurant, and a place to put on the map.\n\nThe staff are friendly and speak Korean well, so you can eat and go with comfort during the trip. Next time I'd like to eat high tongue :)\nRead more\nTranslated from Korean\nShow original\nWritten April 1, 2025",
